arXiv:2510.06149v1 [stat.ML] 07 Oct 2025</div>
</div><div class="ltx_page_content">
<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line">
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning</h1>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Hwanwoo Kim<sup id="id1" class="ltx_sup">†</sup>
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span>Department of Statistical Science, Duke University
</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Dongkyu Derek Cho<sup id="id2" class="ltx_sup">†</sup>
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span>Department of Statistical Science, Duke University
</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Eric Laber
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span>Department of Statistical Science, Duke University
</span></span></span></span></div>
<div class="ltx_dates">August 24, 2026</div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">Temporal difference (TD) learning is a cornerstone of reinforcement learning. In the average-reward setting, standard TD(<math id="abstract1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) is
highly sensitive to the choice of step-size and thus requires careful tuning to maintain numerical stability. We introduce
average-reward implicit TD(<math id="abstract1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>), which employs an implicit fixed point update to provide data-adaptive stabilization while
preserving the per iteration computational complexity of standard average-reward TD(<math id="abstract1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>). In contrast to prior finite-time
analyses of average-reward TD(<math id="abstract1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>), which impose restrictive step-size conditions, we establish finite-time error bounds for the
implicit variant under substantially weaker step-size requirements. Empirically, average-reward implicit TD(<math id="abstract1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) operates
reliably over a much broader range of step-sizes and exhibits markedly improved numerical stability. This enables more efficient
policy evaluation and policy learning, highlighting its effectiveness as a robust alternative to average-reward TD(<math id="abstract1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
  
</div><span id="footnotex1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnotetext"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">$\dagger$</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">$\dagger$</sup><span class="ltx_note_type">footnotetext: </span>equal contribution</span></span></span>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Temporal difference (TD) learning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite> is a core component of modern reinforcement learning (RL), combining
the strengths of Monte Carlo sampling and dynamic programming thereby enabling efficient value estimation from state-action-reward
trajectories exhibiting Markovian dependence. As a foundational method, TD learning underlies many RL algorithms and has been
successfully applied across diverse domains, including robotics <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite>, financial decision-making
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>, and games <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite>. While originally developed in the discounted-reward
setting, TD learning has since been adapted to the average-reward setting <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>, which can be more
natural in many applications <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>, <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>, <a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Despite its widespread use and practical relevance, standard average-reward TD(<math id="S1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>)
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite> is sensitive to step-size selection.
From a theoretical standpoint,
stability is certified by finite-time error bounds, and existing analyses establish such bounds only in
small step-size regimes <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>]</cite>.
In practice, larger step-sizes can accelerate learning
but at the risk of numerical instability;
conversely, smaller step
sizes are more numerically stable but can also yield slower learning.
This stability–efficiency trade-off motivates methods that preserve the
simplicity of the average-reward TD(<math id="S1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) while substantially expanding the range of step-sizes
for which learning remains stable. We address this sensitivity by proposing an average-reward implicit
TD(<math id="S1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) with finite-time error guarantees under substantially less restrictive step-size
conditions.
In addition, the proposed algorithm retains the
computational complexity of standard
average-reward TD(<math id="S1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<section id="S1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.1 </span>Related Literature</h3>

<section id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Discounted-Reward Setting.</h5>

<div id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Almost sure convergence of TD(<math id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) with linear function
approximation was first established in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite>. Subsequent work derived finite-time error bounds under both i.i.d. data streams <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite> and Markovian samples,
using projection-based mean-path analysis <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>, Lyapunov-function arguments
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>, and induction-based proofs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>. In addition, TD-type
methods formulated as two-time scale stochastic approximation algorithms—used for off-policy
evaluation in the discounted setting—have been analyzed in
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>, <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>, <a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Despite the aforementioned theoretical developments in the discounted-reward setting, classical TD
methods typically require restrictive step-size conditions
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>, <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite> and display marked empirical
sensitivity: larger steps may accelerate progress but risk divergence, whereas smaller steps improve
stability at the cost of substantially slower convergence
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>, <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>. A principled remedy is to use implicit stochastic
updates that recast the recursion as a fixed-point equation, providing data-adaptive stabilization,
as shown in the stochastic optimization literature <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>, <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>, <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>.
Building on this principle in reinforcement learning, recent work establishes
asymptotic and finite-time error bounds
for implicit variants of discounted TD in both on- and off-policy tasks without restrictive step-size requirements <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>.
Experiments further show improved numerical stability in both policy evaluation and control tasks.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Average-Reward Setting.</h5>

<div id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For foundations, background, and developments in average-reward policy evaluation, we refer to
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>, <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>, <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>, <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, <a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>, <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>.
The first convergence analysis specific to average-reward TD(<math id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) with linear feature
approximation is due to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>, under the assumption that the
span of the feature vector does not include the constant vector of all ones
(see Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> for additional discussion).
Under the same assumption, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>]</cite> established
asymptotic convergence of the average-reward LSPE(<math id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>), a least-squares based alternative to
the average-reward TD(<math id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>). Relaxing the aforementioned feature space restriction, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite> derived finite-time bounds for average-reward TD(<math id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) with both
constant and linearly decaying step-sizes (i.e., <math id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\text{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mtext>th</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\text{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> step-size <math id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\propto 1/t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\propto 1/t</annotation></semantics></math>), while imposing a restrictive condition on the initial step-size. More recent progress on average-reward
off-policy evaluation with function approximation includes an asymptotically convergent tabular off-policy TD algorithm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite> and extensions of gradient TD methods
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>, <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite> for average-reward off-policy evaluation tasks with linear function approximation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>. Furthermore, TD-style methods for estimating a policy’s asymptotic variance of the cumulative
reward in average-reward setting are developed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.2 </span>Contributions</h3>

<div id="S1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We show that the step-size sensitivity of TD(<math id="S1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>), which has been
well documented in the discounted setting
also arises in the average-reward setting.
To mitigate this sensitivity,
we adopt the implicit stochastic update framework to construct
average-reward implicit TD(<math id="S1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>). We
establish finite-time error bounds under markedly weaker step-size conditions
than those in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>, and we demonstrate
that this relaxation enables computationally efficient policy evaluation and learning across a range
of examples. The primary contributions of our work are summarized as follows.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We propose average-reward implicit TD(<math id="S1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>), which is more robust to step-size choice than the standard average-reward TD(<math id="S1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide finite-time error bounds under both constant and diminishing step-sizes, substantially relaxing the step-size conditions required by existing bounds for standard average-reward TD(<math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>, thereby explaining the improved numerical stability of the implicit variant.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the case of a diminishing step-size, we establish the first finite-time
error bounds in the average-reward setting for step-size sequences of the form <math id="S1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}\propto t^{-s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∝</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}\propto t^{-s}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, covering both square-summable (<math id="S1.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&gt;1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&gt;1/2</annotation></semantics></math>) and non-square-summable (<math id="S1.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;s\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;s\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>) regimes, thereby further broadening the admissible family of step-sizes.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We empirically demonstrate the robustness and efficiency of the proposed method through comprehensive experiments in both policy evaluation and control tasks.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Policy Evaluation in the Average-Reward Setting</h2>

<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Problem Formulation.</h5>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider an infinite‐horizon Markov decision process (MDP) defined by a finite state space <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, a finite action space
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, a bounded reward function <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r:\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}\to[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r:\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}\to[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, and a transition
function <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p:\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}\times\mathcal{S}\to[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p:\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{A}\times\mathcal{S}\to[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under a deterministic stationary
policy <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu:\mathcal{S}\rightarrow\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu:\mathcal{S}\rightarrow\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, at time <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> with a
current state <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\mu}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\mu}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the agent will take an action <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\mu}_{t}=\mu(S^{\mu}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\mu}_{t}=\mu(S^{\mu}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>,
receive a reward <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\mu}_{t}=r(S^{\mu}_{t},A^{\mu}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\mu}_{t}=r(S^{\mu}_{t},A^{\mu}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, and transition to
next state
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\mu}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\mu}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> according to the probability distribution
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(\cdot|S^{\mu}_{t},A^{\mu}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\cdot|S^{\mu}_{t},A^{\mu}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. The resulting state sequence
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{S^{\mu}_{t}\right\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{S^{\mu}_{t}\right\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> induced
by the policy <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> forms a Markov chain with one‐step transition probabilities
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p^{\mu}\left(S^{\mu}_{t+1}|S^{\mu}_{t}\right)=p\left\{S^{\mu}_{t+1}|S^{\mu}_{t},A^{\mu}_{t}=\mu(S^{\mu}_{t})\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\mu}\left(S^{\mu}_{t+1}|S^{\mu}_{t}\right)=p\left\{S^{\mu}_{t+1}|S^{\mu}_{t},A^{\mu}_{t}=\mu(S^{\mu}_{t})\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">
                    †
                  †\dagger</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">
                    †
                  †\dagger</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><math id="footnote1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dagger" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>†</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dagger</annotation></semantics></math></span>
              
              
              
            Since any Markov reward process arises from an MDP under a fixed policy, the general MDP setting covers the Markov reward process case.</span></span></span>
To simplify notation, let
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}=\{1,2,\cdots,|\mathcal{S}|\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}=\{1,2,\cdots,|\mathcal{S}|\}</annotation></semantics></math>
and define time-homogeneous transition probability matrix
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{P}^{\mu}=\bigl[P^{\mu}_{ij}\bigr]_{i,j=1}^{|\mathcal{S}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{P}^{\mu}=\bigl[P^{\mu}_{ij}\bigr]_{i,j=1}^{|\mathcal{S}|}</annotation></semantics></math>
with
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\mu}_{ij}=p^{\mu}\left\{S^{\mu}_{t+1}=j\mid S^{\mu}_{t}=i\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\mu}_{ij}=p^{\mu}\left\{S^{\mu}_{t+1}=j\mid S^{\mu}_{t}=i\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Likewise, let
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{r}^{\mu}=\left[r\{1,\mu(1)\},\cdots,r\{|\mathcal{S}|,\mu(|\mathcal{S}|)\}\right]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒓</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{r}^{\mu}=\left[r\{1,\mu(1)\},\cdots,r\{|\mathcal{S}|,\mu(|\mathcal{S}|)\}\right]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>
be the reward vector.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">One way to characterize the long-term performance of a given policy <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is via its average-reward, defined for each initial state <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="S2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{\mu}(s):=\lim_{T\to\infty}\frac{1}{T}\mathbb{E}^{\mu}\left(\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}R^{\mu}_{t}\Bigm|S^{\mu}_{0}=s\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{\mu}(s):=\lim_{T\to\infty}\frac{1}{T}\mathbb{E}^{\mu}\left(\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}R^{\mu}_{t}\Bigm|S^{\mu}_{0}=s\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where the expectation is taken over the randomness associated with the Markov chain <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{S^{\mu}_{t}\right\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{S^{\mu}_{t}\right\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> induced by the policy <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>. Although the
average-reward provides a natural evaluation criterion for <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, the limit need not exist in general (see, e.g., Chapter 8 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite>). To guarantee the existence and uniqueness of the average-reward, it is common to make the following assumption.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 2.1</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The Markov chain <math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{S^{\mu}_{t}\right\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{S^{\mu}_{t}\right\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> is irreducible and aperiodic.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Under Assumption <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption 2.1. ‣ Problem Formulation. ‣ 2 Policy Evaluation in the Average-Reward Setting ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>, the chain has a unique stationary distribution
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mu}=(\pi^{\mu}_{i})_{i=1}^{|\mathcal{S}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mu}=(\pi^{\mu}_{i})_{i=1}^{|\mathcal{S}|}</annotation></semantics></math>
satisfying
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mu}}^{\top}\boldsymbol{P}^{\mu}={\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mu}}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>𝝅</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>μ</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝝅</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>μ</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mu}}^{\top}\boldsymbol{P}^{\mu}={\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mu}}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mu}_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mu}_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>. Under the same assumption, one can further show that the average-reward is independent of the initial state <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>; that is,
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{\mu}(s)={\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mu}}^{\top}\boldsymbol{r}^{\mu},~\forall s\in\mathcal{S}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>𝝅</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>μ</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒓</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{\mu}(s)={\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mu}}^{\top}\boldsymbol{r}^{\mu},~\forall s\in\mathcal{S}.</annotation></semantics></math>
Unlike its discounted counterpart, the average-reward criterion carries no information about the relative desirability of individual states. To quantify long-run, state-dependent performance under a stationary policy <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, we introduce the basic differential value function <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\mu}:\mathcal{S}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\mu}:\mathcal{S}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\mu}(s):=\mathbb{E}^{\mu}\left\{\sum_{t=0}^{\infty}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\omega^{\mu}\right)\Bigm|S^{\mu}_{0}=s\right\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\mu}(s):=\mathbb{E}^{\mu}\left\{\sum_{t=0}^{\infty}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\omega^{\mu}\right)\Bigm|S^{\mu}_{0}=s\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">which measures the relative advantage (or disadvantage) of starting in state <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>. Accordingly, the quantities of interest are the 1) average reward: <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ω</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> and 2) pairwise contrast: <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\mu}(s)-v^{\mu}(s^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\mu}(s)-v^{\mu}(s^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s,s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s,s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>
which captures the comparative long-run performance of states <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s,s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s,s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In high-dimensional or continuous state spaces, a common strategy is to use linear function approximation, where we model the pairwise difference
as</p>
<table id="S2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\mu}(s)-v^{\mu}(s^{\prime})\approx\{\boldsymbol{\phi}(s)-\boldsymbol{\phi}(s^{\prime})\}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\theta}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\mu}(s)-v^{\mu}(s^{\prime})\approx\{\boldsymbol{\phi}(s)-\boldsymbol{\phi}(s^{\prime})\}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">with a user-chosen feature map <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\phi}(s)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\phi}(s)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>
and weights <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Because adding a
constant to <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\mu}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\mu}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> leaves all differences unchanged, it suffices to
learn <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\mu}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\mu}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> up to an additive constant. Let
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Phi}\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{S}|\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Phi}\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{S}|\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the feature
matrix whose <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i^{\text{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>i</mi><mtext>th</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{\text{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> row is <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\phi}(i)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\phi}(i)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{M}:=\mathrm{diag}(\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mu})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{M}:=\mathrm{diag}(\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mu}).</annotation></semantics></math> Writing
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v}^{\mu}:=[v^{\mu}(1),\ldots,v^{\mu}(|\mathcal{S}|)]^{\top}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v}^{\mu}:=[v^{\mu}(1),\ldots,v^{\mu}(|\mathcal{S}|)]^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math>
one has the series representation
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v}^{\mu}=\sum_{t=0}^{\infty}(\boldsymbol{P}^{\mu})^{t}\left(\boldsymbol{r}^{\mu}-\omega^{\mu}\boldsymbol{e}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒓</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒆</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v}^{\mu}=\sum_{t=0}^{\infty}(\boldsymbol{P}^{\mu})^{t}\left(\boldsymbol{r}^{\mu}-\omega^{\mu}\boldsymbol{e}\right),</annotation></semantics></math>
where <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{e}</annotation></semantics></math> is the all-ones vector. With the weighted norm <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\boldsymbol{x}\|_{\boldsymbol{M}}:=(\boldsymbol{x}^{\top}\boldsymbol{M}\boldsymbol{x})^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>𝑴</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\boldsymbol{x}\|_{\boldsymbol{M}}:=(\boldsymbol{x}^{\top}\boldsymbol{M}\boldsymbol{x})^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>, our second goal translates to finding <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the weighted discrepancy</p>
<table id="S2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{c\in\mathbb{R}}\bigl\|\boldsymbol{\Phi}\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}-(\boldsymbol{v}^{\mu}+c\boldsymbol{e})\bigr\|_{\boldsymbol{M}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒆</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi>𝑴</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{c\in\mathbb{R}}\bigl\|\boldsymbol{\Phi}\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}-(\boldsymbol{v}^{\mu}+c\boldsymbol{e})\bigr\|_{\boldsymbol{M}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">is small. This quantity is zero when the feature space contains a constant shift of the basic differential value function (i.e., the differential value function). When the weighted discrepancy is small, it indicates that <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\phi}(s)^{\top}\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\phi}(s)^{\top}\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> approximates <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\mu}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\mu}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> up to an additive constant, so the estimation of the contrasts <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\mu}(s)-v^{\mu}(s^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\mu}(s)-v^{\mu}(s^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is correspondingly accurate, improving as the discrepancy decreases.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Average-Reward TD(<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) with Linear Approximation.</h5>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The average-reward TD<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> algorithm
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite> is a widely used stochastic-approximation
method to achieve the aforementioned goals. At the <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\text{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mtext>th</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\text{th}}</annotation></semantics></math>
iteration, the average‐reward TD(<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) algorithm maintains both
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\omega}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\omega}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, an estimate of the average-reward <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ω</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>, and an
estimate <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> of the optimal weight
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. With non-increasing positive step-sizes
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t},\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t},\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and exponential weighting parameter
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in[0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in[0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, the update rules are given by</p>
<table id="S2.E1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S2.E1X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E1X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E1X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\alpha_{t}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\alpha_{t}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E1Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E1Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E1Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}\delta_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}\delta_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where the eligibility trace <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and TD error <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> are</p>
<table id="S2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{z}_{t}=\sum_{i=0}^{t}\lambda^{t-i}\boldsymbol{\phi}\left(S^{\mu}_{i}\right),~~\delta_{t}=R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+{\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}}^{\top}\left\{\boldsymbol{\phi}\left(S^{\mu}_{t+1}\right)-\boldsymbol{\phi}\left(S^{\mu}_{t}\right)\right\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.827em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{z}_{t}=\sum_{i=0}^{t}\lambda^{t-i}\boldsymbol{\phi}\left(S^{\mu}_{i}\right),~~\delta_{t}=R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+{\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}}^{\top}\left\{\boldsymbol{\phi}\left(S^{\mu}_{t+1}\right)-\boldsymbol{\phi}\left(S^{\mu}_{t}\right)\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">each respectively representing the geometrically weighted average of past feature vectors at visited states and the one‐step TD error, which measures how the reward (after subtracting the current average‐reward estimate <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\omega}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\omega}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>) plus the estimated value of the next state differs from the current value estimate.
We restrict our attention to a single-time-scale average-reward TD(<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) algorithm by assuming <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}=c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}=c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with fixed <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\alpha}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\alpha}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>, <a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>]</cite>. Exploring distinct decay rates, an instance of the two-time-scale stochastic approximation framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>, is interesting but outside our scope.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step-Size Sensitivity.</h5>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Despite its foundational role in RL, standard average-reward TD(<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) suffers from numerical
sensitivity to step-size selection. To illustrate this issue, we present a simple numerical example.
We consider a Markov reward process (MRP) with <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|=100</annotation></semantics></math> states and evaluate the
performance of average-reward TD(<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) learning with hyperparameter configuration
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(c_{\alpha},\lambda)=(1.0,0.25)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.25</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c_{\alpha},\lambda)=(1.0,0.25)</annotation></semantics></math> with a predetermined constant step-size
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}=\beta_{0}\in(0,2),~\forall t\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}=\beta_{0}\in(0,2),~\forall t\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. The objective is to estimate both
the optimal weight <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and the average-reward <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ω</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>. Detailed descriptions of
the evaluation criterion (loss function) and experimental setting are provided in
Sections <a href="#S4" title="4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and <a href="#S5" title="5 Numerical Experiments ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S2.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ Step-Size Sensitivity. ‣ 2 Policy Evaluation in the Average-Reward Setting ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> illustrates the instability induced by step-size choices. The left panel shows a non-monotonic trend in
performance: overly small step-sizes (e.g., <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{0}&lt;0.20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{0}&lt;0.20</annotation></semantics></math>) lead to slow convergence, while a modest increase in step-size causes
the loss function values to grow rapidly. The right panel presents the result for a moderately large step-size (<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{0}=1.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{0}=1.8</annotation></semantics></math>),
where the average-reward TD(<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) iterates exhibit oscillatory behavior. These empirical findings highlight the sensitivity of
the TD learning to step-size selection and motivate the need for algorithms that are robust to such choices. In the following
sections, we propose and analyze one such approach.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F1" class="ltx_figure">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 1</span>: </span><span id="S2.F1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Sensitivity of average-reward TD(<math id="S2.F1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) to the choice of step-size with exponential weighting parameter <math id="S2.F1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0.25</annotation></semantics></math> and step-size ratio <math id="S2.F1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\alpha}=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\alpha}=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>. The solid line denotes the mean, and the shaded region indicates the 95% confidence interval. </span></figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S2.F1.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.06149v1/figure/demonstration/DEMO_summary_plot_FULL_lamb0.25_alpha1.00.png" id="S2.F1.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/417;" width="476" height="417" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F1.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="S2.F1.sf1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Performance of average-reward TD(<math id="S2.F1.sf1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) for step-sizes <math id="S2.F1.sf1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> ranging from <math id="S2.F1.sf1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.F1.sf1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S2.F1.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.06149v1/figure/demonstration/DEMO_alpha_1.8_full.png" id="S2.F1.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/417;" width="476" height="417" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F1.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="S2.F1.sf2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Performance over iterations with step-size <math id="S2.F1.sf2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{0}=1.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{0}=1.8</annotation></semantics></math>, showing no improvement.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Average-Reward Implicit TD(<math id="S3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>)</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As we have seen in the previous section, average‐reward TD(<math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) demands carefully tuned step-sizes for stability. Implicit stochastic recursions, developed for stochastic gradient descent <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>, <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>, <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>, <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite> and more recently extended to discounted‐reward on- and off‐policy TD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>, rewrite each update as a fixed‐point equation by allowing the gradient or TD error to depend on the new iterate. This reformulation automatically induces an adaptive shrinkage in the effective step-size, vastly improving numerical stability without increasing computational complexity. Building on this idea, we introduce the average‐reward implicit TD(<math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>), which retains the simplicity and efficiency of standard average‐reward TD(<math id="S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) while supporting more flexible step-size choices with finite-time error guarantees. In this section, we propose a novel average‐reward TD(<math id="S3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) algorithm that incorporates implicit updates into its recursive structure.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To derive implicit average-reward TD(<math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) updates, recall the update rule for <math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> given in (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In Average-Reward TD(𝜆) with Linear Approximation. ‣ 2 Policy Evaluation in the Average-Reward Setting ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>):</p>
<table id="S3.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}&amp;=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\\
&amp;=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}\left\{R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-(\boldsymbol{z}_{t}-\lambda\boldsymbol{z}_{t-1})^{\top}\boldsymbol{\theta}_{t}\right\}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\\
&amp;=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\lambda\boldsymbol{z}_{t-1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{z}_{t}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t},\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}&amp;=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\\
&amp;=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}\left\{R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-(\boldsymbol{z}_{t}-\lambda\boldsymbol{z}_{t-1})^{\top}\boldsymbol{\theta}_{t}\right\}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\\
&amp;=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\lambda\boldsymbol{z}_{t-1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{z}_{t}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t},\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where we have used the identity <math id="S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}=\boldsymbol{z}_{t}-\lambda\boldsymbol{z}_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}=\boldsymbol{z}_{t}-\lambda\boldsymbol{z}_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> in the second equality. At time <math id="S3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, we update <math id="S3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\omega}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\omega}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> using a rule that depends on both the current iterate <math id="S3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\widehat{\omega}_{t},\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widehat{\omega}_{t},\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and their updated values <math id="S3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\widehat{\omega}_{t+1},\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widehat{\omega}_{t+1},\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{\omega}_{t}+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}(R^{\mu}_{t}-{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{\omega}_{t}+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}(R^{\mu}_{t}-{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\lambda\boldsymbol{z}_{t-1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{z}_{t}^{\top}{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}})\boldsymbol{z}_{t}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\lambda\boldsymbol{z}_{t-1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{z}_{t}^{\top}{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}})\boldsymbol{z}_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Solving the above recursions (<a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3 Average-Reward Implicit TD(𝜆) ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) and (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3 Average-Reward Implicit TD(𝜆) ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) admits the update rule for the average-reward implicit TD(<math id="S3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) algorithm. Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Average-Reward Implicit TD(𝜆) ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> below characterizes the average-reward implicit TD(<math id="S3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) algorithm, and its proof is given in the supplementary materials.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Average-reward implicit TD(<math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) updates given in (<a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3 Average-Reward Implicit TD(𝜆) ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) and (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3 Average-Reward Implicit TD(𝜆) ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) can be expressed as</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\frac{c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\frac{c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\frac{\beta_{t}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|_{2}^{2}}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\frac{\beta_{t}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|_{2}^{2}}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The update rule in Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3 Average-Reward Implicit TD(𝜆) ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> highlights a key mechanism underlying the robustness of the average-reward implicit TD(<math id="S3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) learning. Unlike the standard average-reward TD(<math id="S3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) methods, at each step <math id="S3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, the implicit updates dynamically rescale the step-size based on the magnitude of the eligibility trace as well as the step-size ratio parameter. Such shrinkage arises naturally from the implicit update mechanism, reducing the burden of laborious tuning. Importantly, the implicit algorithm has the same space and time complexity as the standard method in the average-reward setting, making it a practical replacement without additional computational burden or implementation difficulty. The benefits of this mechanism will be further clarified in the forthcoming theoretical analysis and subsequently illustrated
through a suite of numerical examples.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To further enhance numerical stability and facilitate theoretical analysis of the average‑reward implicit TD<math id="S3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> algorithm, we introduce a projection step that forces each iterate <math id="S3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}:=[\widehat{\omega}_{t},\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}:=[\widehat{\omega}_{t},\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> to lie within the Euclidean ball of radius <math id="S3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> by enforcing the constraints
<math id="S3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\boldsymbol{\Theta}\|_{2}\leq R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\boldsymbol{\Theta}\|_{2}\leq R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Such projection‐based stabilization is well‐studied in both the stochastic optimization and reinforcement learning literatures, and numerous theoretical results have been established <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>, <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>, <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, <a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>, <a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>, <a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>]</cite>. In practice, one can choose <math id="S3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently large to ensure the limit point of <math id="S3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in the Euclidean ball of radius <math id="S3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}</annotation></semantics></math>. A complete algorithmic description of the average-reward implicit TD(<math id="S3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) is provided in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3 Average-Reward Implicit TD(𝜆) ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Average-reward implicit TD(<math id="alg1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) (with projection)</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> exponential weighting parameter <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in[0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in[0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, basis functions <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\boldsymbol{\phi}_{k}\}_{k=1}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\boldsymbol{\phi}_{k}\}_{k=1}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, step-size <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\beta_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\beta_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math>, step-size ratio parameter <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, projection radius <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
            
            
           Initialize: <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\omega}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\omega}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\mu}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\mu}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and eligibility trace <math id="alg1.l2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{z}_{-1}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{z}_{-1}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>  <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0,1,2,\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0,1,2,\dots</annotation></semantics></math>  <span id="alg1.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
            
            
            Receive data: <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S^{\mu}_{t},R^{\mu}_{t},S^{\mu}_{t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S^{\mu}_{t},R^{\mu}_{t},S^{\mu}_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
            
            
            Get TD error: 
<table id="S3.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\delta_{t}=R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}(S^{\mu}_{t+1})^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\phi}(S^{\mu}_{t})^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta_{t}=R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}(S^{\mu}_{t+1})^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\phi}(S^{\mu}_{t})^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
            
            
            Update eligibility trace: <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{z}_{t}=\lambda\boldsymbol{z}_{t-1}+\boldsymbol{\phi}(S^{\mu}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{z}_{t}=\lambda\boldsymbol{z}_{t-1}+\boldsymbol{\phi}(S^{\mu}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
            
            
            Update parameters: 
<table id="S3.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\frac{c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\frac{c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\frac{\beta_{t}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|_{2}^{2}}\delta_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\frac{\beta_{t}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|_{2}^{2}}\delta_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
            
            
            For projected average-reward implicit TD(<math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>):
if <math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\widehat{\omega}_{t+1})^{2}+\|\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}\|^{2}\geq R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widehat{\omega}_{t+1})^{2}+\|\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}\|^{2}\geq R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,

<table id="S3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{(\widehat{\omega}_{t+1})^{2}+\|\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}\|_{2}^{2}}}\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{(\widehat{\omega}_{t+1})^{2}+\|\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}\|_{2}^{2}}}\widehat{\omega}_{t+1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{(\widehat{\omega}_{t+1})^{2}+\|\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}\|_{2}^{2}}}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{(\widehat{\omega}_{t+1})^{2}+\|\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}\|_{2}^{2}}}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Theoretical Analysis</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide a theoretical analysis of the average-reward implicit TD(<math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) algorithm incorporating a projection
step. We first assume that the columns of <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math> are linearly independent, which implies that the basis functions
span a <math id="S4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional feature space. Such an assumption ensures that redundant basis functions can be removed without loss of
expressiveness. Hereafter, we use <math id="S4.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the Euclidean norm for vectors and operator norm for matrices. We assume that
the feature vectors are normalized so that <math id="S4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\boldsymbol{\phi}(i)\|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\boldsymbol{\phi}(i)\|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>. Lastly,
<math id="S4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}^{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes expectation with respect to the Markov chain <math id="S4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{S^{\mu}_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{S^{\mu}_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> under policy <math id="S4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> with a fixed <math id="S4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\mu}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\mu}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="S4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}^{\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mu}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}^{\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mu}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes expectation with respect to the stationary distribution of this chain.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To facilitate our analysis, we formulate the average-reward TD(<math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) update into a matrix notation form, given by</p>
<table id="S4.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{bmatrix}\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}\\
\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{bmatrix}\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}\\
\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}\widehat{\omega}_{t}\\
\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\end{bmatrix}+\beta_{t}\begin{bmatrix}-c_{\alpha}&amp;0\\
-{\boldsymbol{z}_{t}}&{\boldsymbol{z}_{t}}(\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top})\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}\widehat{\omega}_{t}\\
\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\end{bmatrix}+\begin{bmatrix}c_{\alpha}R^{\mu}_{t}\\
{R^{\mu}_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}}\end{bmatrix}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}\widehat{\omega}_{t}\\
\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\end{bmatrix}+\beta_{t}\begin{bmatrix}-c_{\alpha}&amp;0\\
-{\boldsymbol{z}_{t}}&amp;{\boldsymbol{z}_{t}}(\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top})\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}\widehat{\omega}_{t}\\
\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\end{bmatrix}+\begin{bmatrix}c_{\alpha}R^{\mu}_{t}\\
{R^{\mu}_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}}\end{bmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which can be succinctly written as</p>
<table id="S4.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t+1}=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}\{\boldsymbol{A}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t})\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\boldsymbol{b}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t})\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t+1}=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}\{\boldsymbol{A}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t})\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\boldsymbol{b}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t})\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">and its implicit version is given by</p>
<table id="S4.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t+1}=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\boldsymbol{D}_{t}\{\boldsymbol{A}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t})\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\boldsymbol{b}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t})\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t+1}=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\boldsymbol{D}_{t}\{\boldsymbol{A}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t})\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\boldsymbol{b}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t})\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p2.4" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="S4.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}:=\begin{bmatrix}\widehat{\omega}_{t}\\
\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\end{bmatrix},\quad\boldsymbol{A}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t}):=\begin{bmatrix}-c_{\alpha}&amp;0\\
-{\boldsymbol{z}_{t}}&{\boldsymbol{z}_{t}}(\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top})\end{bmatrix}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}:=\begin{bmatrix}\widehat{\omega}_{t}\\
\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\end{bmatrix},\quad\boldsymbol{A}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t}):=\begin{bmatrix}-c_{\alpha}&amp;0\\
-{\boldsymbol{z}_{t}}&amp;{\boldsymbol{z}_{t}}(\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top})\end{bmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{b}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t}):=\begin{bmatrix}c_{\alpha}R^{\mu}_{t}\\
{R^{\mu}_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}}\end{bmatrix},\quad\boldsymbol{D}_{t}:=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{1}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}&amp;0\\
0&amp;\frac{1}{1+\beta_{t}||\boldsymbol{z}_{t}||^{2}}\boldsymbol{I}_{d}\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{b}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t}):=\begin{bmatrix}c_{\alpha}R^{\mu}_{t}\\
{R^{\mu}_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}}\end{bmatrix},\quad\boldsymbol{D}_{t}:=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{1}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}&amp;0\\
0&amp;\frac{1}{1+\beta_{t}||\boldsymbol{z}_{t}||^{2}}\boldsymbol{I}_{d}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p2.5" class="ltx_p">with <math id="S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{X}_{t}:=(S^{\mu}_{t},S^{\mu}_{t+1},\boldsymbol{z}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{X}_{t}:=(S^{\mu}_{t},S^{\mu}_{t+1},\boldsymbol{z}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Under suitable technical conditions, if <math id="S4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{A}:=\mathbb{E}^{\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mu}}[\boldsymbol{A}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{A}:=\mathbb{E}^{\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mu}}[\boldsymbol{A}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t})]</annotation></semantics></math> is negative definite, results from stochastic approximation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> imply that the iterate <math id="S4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> converges almost surely to <math id="S4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{*}=[\omega^{\mu},\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{*}=[\omega^{\mu},\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, which solves <math id="S4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{A}\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{*}+\boldsymbol{b}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝒃</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{A}\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{*}+\boldsymbol{b}=0</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{b}:=\mathbb{E}^{\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mu}}[\boldsymbol{b}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{b}:=\mathbb{E}^{\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mu}}[\boldsymbol{b}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t})]</annotation></semantics></math>. Earlier work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite> established almost sure convergence <math id="S4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> by assuming <math id="S4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is negative definite (up to left multiplication by a diagonal matrix). However, such an assumption excludes cases where the feature matrix <math id="S4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math> can yield value predictions that are constant across all states, i.e., when <math id="S4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{e}</annotation></semantics></math> lies in the column space of <math id="S4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To relax the aforementioned assumption, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite> considered an auxiliary iterate <math id="S4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\widehat{\omega}_{t},\Pi_{\mathbb{O}}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝕆</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\widehat{\omega}_{t},\Pi_{\mathbb{O}}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\mathbb{O}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝕆</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\mathbb{O}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes projection onto <math id="S4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{O}</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as the orthogonal complement of
<math id="S4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{\boldsymbol{\Phi},\boldsymbol{e}}:=\operatorname{span}\{\boldsymbol{\theta}:\boldsymbol{\Phi}\boldsymbol{\theta}=\boldsymbol{e}\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒆</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>span</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒆</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{\boldsymbol{\Phi},\boldsymbol{e}}:=\operatorname{span}\{\boldsymbol{\theta}:\boldsymbol{\Phi}\boldsymbol{\theta}=\boldsymbol{e}\}.</annotation></semantics></math>
Projecting onto <math id="S4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{O}</annotation></semantics></math> thus removes the constant-shift direction, i.e., the component of <math id="S4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Phi}\boldsymbol{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Phi}\boldsymbol{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> aligned with the all-ones vector direction. Such component adds the same constant to every state’s value prediction and does not affect estimates of value contrasts <math id="S4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\mu}(s)-v^{\mu}(s^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\mu}(s)-v^{\mu}(s^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. Accordingly, it is natural to assess performance using the projected iterate <math id="S4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\mathbb{O}}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝕆</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\mathbb{O}}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> since any change in <math id="S4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> along <math id="S4.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{span}\{\boldsymbol{e}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>span</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝒆</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{span}\{\boldsymbol{e}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is not identifiable in the average-reward setting and can be ignored. Furthermore, on <math id="S4.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝕆</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{O}</annotation></semantics></math>, one can restore strict negative definiteness of the matrix <math id="S4.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, formalized as Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 4.1 (Lemma 2 of []). ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> below.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lemma 2 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{M}=\text{diag}\left(\pi^{\mu}_{1},\cdots,\pi^{\mu}_{|\mathcal{S}|}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{M}=\text{diag}\left(\pi^{\mu}_{1},\cdots,\pi^{\mu}_{|\mathcal{S}|}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{P}^{(\lambda)}=(1-\lambda)\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}\lambda^{m}(\boldsymbol{P}^{\mu})^{m+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{P}^{(\lambda)}=(1-\lambda)\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}\lambda^{m}(\boldsymbol{P}^{\mu})^{m+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under Assumption <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption 2.1. ‣ Problem Formulation. ‣ 2 Policy Evaluation in the Average-Reward Setting ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta:=\hskip-8.53581pt\min_{\|\boldsymbol{\theta}\|=1,\boldsymbol{\theta}\in\mathbb{O}}\boldsymbol{\theta}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\boldsymbol{\Phi}}^{\top}\boldsymbol{M}\left(\boldsymbol{I}-\boldsymbol{P}^{(\lambda)}\right)\boldsymbol{\boldsymbol{\Phi}}\boldsymbol{\theta}&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕆</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝑷</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta:=\hskip-8.53581pt\min_{\|\boldsymbol{\theta}\|=1,\boldsymbol{\theta}\in\mathbb{O}}\boldsymbol{\theta}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\boldsymbol{\Phi}}^{\top}\boldsymbol{M}\left(\boldsymbol{I}-\boldsymbol{P}^{(\lambda)}\right)\boldsymbol{\boldsymbol{\Phi}}\boldsymbol{\theta}&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In addition, for <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\alpha}\geq\Delta+\sqrt{\frac{1}{\Delta^{2}(1-\lambda)^{4}}-\frac{1}{(1-\lambda)^{2}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\alpha}\geq\Delta+\sqrt{\frac{1}{\Delta^{2}(1-\lambda)^{4}}-\frac{1}{(1-\lambda)^{2}}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\top}\boldsymbol{A}\boldsymbol{\Theta}\leq-\frac{\Delta}{2}\|\boldsymbol{\Theta}\|^{2},~~\text{for any}~~\boldsymbol{\Theta}\in\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{O}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚯</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.827em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for any</mtext><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚯</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝕆</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\top}\boldsymbol{A}\boldsymbol{\Theta}\leq-\frac{\Delta}{2}\|\boldsymbol{\Theta}\|^{2},~~\text{for any}~~\boldsymbol{\Theta}\in\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{O}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">With the negative definiteness of the matrix <math id="S4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, the limit point <math id="S4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is assured to be unique and one can then ask how far the auxiliary iterates are from the limit point. Specifically non-asymptotic bounds on <math id="S4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\widehat{\omega}_{t}-\omega^{\mu}\right)^{2}+\left\|\Pi_{\mathbb{O}}\left(\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}\right)\right\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝕆</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\widehat{\omega}_{t}-\omega^{\mu}\right)^{2}+\left\|\Pi_{\mathbb{O}}\left(\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}\right)\right\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> were established both for constant and decreasing step-size schedules <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>. In addition to the finite-time error bounds, the approximation quality of <math id="S4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> within the chosen feature class is captured by the <math id="S4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{M}</annotation></semantics></math>-weighted discrepancy</p>
<table id="S4.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{c\in\mathbb{R}}\|\boldsymbol{\Phi}\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}-(\boldsymbol{v}^{\mu}+c\boldsymbol{e})\|_{\boldsymbol{M}}\;\leq\;\,\tfrac{\inf_{\boldsymbol{\theta}\in\mathbb{R}^{d},\,c\in\mathbb{R}}\|\boldsymbol{\Phi}\boldsymbol{\theta}-(\boldsymbol{v}^{\mu}+c\boldsymbol{e})\|_{\boldsymbol{M}}}{\sqrt{1-c_{\lambda}^{2}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒆</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>𝑴</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.728em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>inf</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒆</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>𝑴</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{c\in\mathbb{R}}\|\boldsymbol{\Phi}\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}-(\boldsymbol{v}^{\mu}+c\boldsymbol{e})\|_{\boldsymbol{M}}\;\leq\;\,\tfrac{\inf_{\boldsymbol{\theta}\in\mathbb{R}^{d},\,c\in\mathbb{R}}\|\boldsymbol{\Phi}\boldsymbol{\theta}-(\boldsymbol{v}^{\mu}+c\boldsymbol{e})\|_{\boldsymbol{M}}}{\sqrt{1-c_{\lambda}^{2}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p5.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="S4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\lambda}\in[0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\lambda}\in[0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\lambda}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\lambda}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S4.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\to 1</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>. Note that the right-hand term involves the best error achievable within the feature class. Thus <math id="S4.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is optimal up to a multiplicative factor, which approaches <math id="S4.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S4.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\to 1</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, if the feature class is rich enough to represent any one differential value function, the best achievable error is zero; that is,
<math id="S4.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{c\in\mathbb{R}}\big\|\boldsymbol{\Phi}\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}-(\boldsymbol{v}^{\mu}+c\boldsymbol{e})\big\|_{\boldsymbol{M}}=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>inf</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒆</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi>𝑴</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{c\in\mathbb{R}}\big\|\boldsymbol{\Phi}\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}-(\boldsymbol{v}^{\mu}+c\boldsymbol{e})\big\|_{\boldsymbol{M}}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Non-asymptotic Analysis of Average-Reward Implicit TD(<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>).</h5>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We are now ready to present finite-time error bounds for average-reward implicit TD(<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) with the projection step, formally stated in Theorems <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4.4. ‣ Non-asymptotic Analysis of Average-Reward Implicit TD(𝜆). ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a> and <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 4.5. ‣ Non-asymptotic Analysis of Average-Reward Implicit TD(𝜆). ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>. Results are provided for both constant and decreasing step-sizes. The bounds are expressed in terms of the negative-definiteness margin <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> from Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 4.1 (Lemma 2 of []). ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, the step-size parameters <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> (ratio: <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}/\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}/\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>), <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (initial step-size), and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> (decay rate) and the mixing time of the underlying Markov process <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{S^{\mu}_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{S^{\mu}_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> whose formal definition is given below.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 4.2</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Mixing Time)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{S_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}\subset\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{S_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}\subset\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> be a Markov chain with stationary distribution <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, its mixing time is the smallest positive integer <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\epsilon}\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\epsilon}\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq\tau_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq\tau_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{s\in\mathcal{S}}d_{\mathrm{TV}}\left\{\mathbb{P}(S_{t}=\cdot\mid S_{0}=s),\pi(\cdot)\right\}\leq\epsilon," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{s\in\mathcal{S}}d_{\mathrm{TV}}\left\{\mathbb{P}(S_{t}=\cdot\mid S_{0}=s),\pi(\cdot)\right\}\leq\epsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{TV}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{TV}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the total variation distance.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 4.3</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption 2.1. ‣ Problem Formulation. ‣ 2 Policy Evaluation in the Average-Reward Setting ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>, the Markov chain <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{S^{\mu}_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{S^{\mu}_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly geometrically ergodic: there exist <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sup_{s\in\mathcal{S}}d_{\mathrm{TV}}\left\{p^{\mu}(S^{\mu}_{t}=\cdot\mid S^{\mu}_{0}=s),\pi^{\mu}_{\cdot}\right\}\leq m\rho^{t}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{s\in\mathcal{S}}d_{\mathrm{TV}}\left\{p^{\mu}(S^{\mu}_{t}=\cdot\mid S^{\mu}_{0}=s),\pi^{\mu}_{\cdot}\right\}\leq m\rho^{t}.</annotation></semantics></math>
Consequently, its mixing time <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> is of order <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}\left(\log\frac{1}{\epsilon}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}\left(\log\frac{1}{\epsilon}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.4</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose the Markov chain <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{S^{\mu}_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{S^{\mu}_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly geometrically ergodic with a rate parameter <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, the step-size ratio parameter is chosen to satisfy <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\alpha}\geq\Delta+\sqrt{\frac{1}{\Delta^{2}(1-\lambda)^{4}}-\frac{1}{(1-\lambda)^{2}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\alpha}\geq\Delta+\sqrt{\frac{1}{\Delta^{2}(1-\lambda)^{4}}-\frac{1}{(1-\lambda)^{2}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the optimal parameter <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{*}\|\leq R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{*}\|\leq R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}</annotation></semantics></math>. With <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in[0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in[0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and constant step-size <math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}=\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}=\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, the iterates of the projected average-reward implicit TD(<math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) algorithm satisfy the following finite-time error bound</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}^{\mu}\left\{\left(\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}-\omega^{\mu}\right)^{2}+\left\|\Pi_{\mathbb{O}}\left(\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}-\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}\right)\right\|^{2}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝕆</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}^{\mu}\left\{\left(\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}-\omega^{\mu}\right)^{2}+\left\|\Pi_{\mathbb{O}}\left(\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}-\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}\right)\right\|^{2}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim(1-\beta\gamma\Delta)^{t+1}\left\{\left(\widehat{\omega}_{0}^{\mu}-\omega^{\mu}\right)^{2}+\left\|\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{0}-\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}\right\|^{2}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim(1-\beta\gamma\Delta)^{t+1}\left\{\left(\widehat{\omega}_{0}^{\mu}-\omega^{\mu}\right)^{2}+\left\|\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{0}-\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}\right\|^{2}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\mathcal{O}\left(\beta\tau_{\beta}+h^{\tau_{\beta}}+\beta\tau_{\beta}th^{t}\right),\quad t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\mathcal{O}\left(\beta\tau_{\beta}+h^{\tau_{\beta}}+\beta\tau_{\beta}th^{t}\right),\quad t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=\max\{1-\beta\gamma\Delta,\rho,\lambda\}~\text{and}~\gamma=\min\left\{\frac{1}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta},\frac{(1-\lambda)^{2}}{(1-\lambda)^{2}+\beta}\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=\max\{1-\beta\gamma\Delta,\rho,\lambda\}~\text{and}~\gamma=\min\left\{\frac{1}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta},\frac{(1-\lambda)^{2}}{(1-\lambda)^{2}+\beta}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.5</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose the Markov chain <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{S^{\mu}_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{S^{\mu}_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly geometrically ergodic with a rate parameter <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, the step-size ratio parameter is chosen to satisfy <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\alpha}\geq\Delta+\sqrt{\frac{1}{\Delta^{2}(1-\lambda)^{4}}-\frac{1}{(1-\lambda)^{2}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\alpha}\geq\Delta+\sqrt{\frac{1}{\Delta^{2}(1-\lambda)^{4}}-\frac{1}{(1-\lambda)^{2}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the optimal parameter <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{*}\|\leq R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{*}\|\leq R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}</annotation></semantics></math>. With <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in[0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in[0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and decreasing step-sizes <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}=\frac{\beta_{0}}{(t+1)^{s}},~s\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}=\frac{\beta_{0}}{(t+1)^{s}},~s\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, the iterates of the projected average-reward implicit TD(<math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) algorithm satisfy the following finite-time error bound</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}^{\mu}\left\{\left(\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}-\omega^{\mu}\right)^{2}+\left\|\Pi_{\mathbb{O}}\left(\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}-\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}\right)\right\|^{2}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝕆</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}^{\mu}\left\{\left(\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}-\omega^{\mu}\right)^{2}+\left\|\Pi_{\mathbb{O}}\left(\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}-\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}\right)\right\|^{2}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\exp\left[-\frac{\Delta\gamma_{0}\beta_{0}}{1-s}\{(1+t)^{1-s}-1\}\right]\left\{\left(\widehat{\omega}_{0}^{\mu}-\omega^{\mu}\right)^{2}+\left\|\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{0}-\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}\right\|^{2}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\exp\left[-\frac{\Delta\gamma_{0}\beta_{0}}{1-s}\{(1+t)^{1-s}-1\}\right]\left\{\left(\widehat{\omega}_{0}^{\mu}-\omega^{\mu}\right)^{2}+\left\|\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{0}-\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}\right\|^{2}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\mathcal{O}\left\{\tau_{\beta_{t}}t\exp\left(-ct^{1-s}\right)+\tau_{\beta_{t}}t^{-s}+q^{\tau_{\beta_{t}}}\right\},\quad t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></msup></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\mathcal{O}\left\{\tau_{\beta_{t}}t\exp\left(-ct^{1-s}\right)+\tau_{\beta_{t}}t^{-s}+q^{\tau_{\beta_{t}}}\right\},\quad t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for some constant <math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=\max\{\rho,\lambda\}~\text{and}~\gamma_{0}=\min\left\{\frac{1}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{0}},\frac{(1-\lambda)^{2}}{(1-\lambda)^{2}+\beta_{0}}\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=\max\{\rho,\lambda\}~\text{and}~\gamma_{0}=\min\left\{\frac{1}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{0}},\frac{(1-\lambda)^{2}}{(1-\lambda)^{2}+\beta_{0}}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 4.6</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Our two theorems substantially relax the restrictive conditions required in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>.</span></p>
<ul id="S4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For constant step-sizes, we establish a finite-time bound without any initial step-size requirements.
By contrast, previous analysis ties the initial step-size to a problem dependent quantity (e.g., </span><math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\beta&lt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\beta&lt;2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) and further
imposes restrictive upper bounds on the step-size as well as the mixing time </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">[</span><a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a><span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">]</span></cite><span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For decaying step-sizes, our theorem accommodates the polynomial schedule of the form </span><math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}=\beta_{0}/(t+1)^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}=\beta_{0}/(t+1)^{s}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for any
</span><math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, not just the </span><math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> rate covered in </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">[</span><a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">]</span></cite><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. In addition, the bounds in </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">[</span><a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">]</span></cite><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> hold
only under extra restrictions, for example, there must exist an index </span><math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> with bounded cumulative step-size up to
</span><math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and all subsequent step-sizes must stay below a problem-dependent threshold.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">These relaxations remove delicate initial step-size conditions and broaden the range of admissible step-size schedules, while still
providing finite-time error guarantees.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Numerical Experiments</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we demonstrate the effectiveness of the proposed average-reward implicit TD(<math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) relative to
standard average-reward TD(<math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) on both policy evaluation and control tasks. All experiments were carried out on Intel(R)
Xeon(R) Gold 6152 CPUs at 2.10 GHz with 32 GB RAM.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Policy Evaluation</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For policy evaluation, we use MRP and the Boyan chain examples; for policy learning, we consider the
access-control and pendulum problems. Performance is quantified by the loss function given by
<math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(\widehat{\omega}_{t}-\omega^{\mu}\bigr)^{2}+\bigl\|\Pi_{\mathbb{O}}(\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\theta}^{\ast})\bigr\|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝕆</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(\widehat{\omega}_{t}-\omega^{\mu}\bigr)^{2}+\bigl\|\Pi_{\mathbb{O}}(\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\theta}^{\ast})\bigr\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math>
A detailed description of how the loss value is computed is provided in the supplementary materials. We
consider both constant and decaying step-size schedules. For decaying schedules, the step-size is held
fixed for the first 150 iterations to promote exploration and then decreased thereafter. Each
configuration is run for <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=2000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=2000</annotation></semantics></math> steps with <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\omega}_{0}^{\mu}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\omega}_{0}^{\mu}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{0}\sim\mathrm{Unif}([-1,1]^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Unif</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{0}\sim\mathrm{Unif}([-1,1]^{d})</annotation></semantics></math>, and results are averaged over 50 independent
trials. We fix the step-size ratio <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\alpha}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\alpha}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and the exponential weighting parameter <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0.25</annotation></semantics></math>. We compare four methods: (i) average-reward standard TD(<math id="S5.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>); (ii) average-reward implicit
TD(<math id="S5.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) without projection; and (iii–iv) average-reward implicit TD(<math id="S5.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) with projection,
using projection radius <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}\in\{1000,\,5000\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1000</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 5000</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}\in\{1000,\,5000\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Full implementation details and
additional experimental results are provided in the supplementary materials.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.1.1 </span>Markov Reward Process</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we study an MRP with <math id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}|=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}|=100</annotation></semantics></math> states; the transition matrix and reward vector are
generated following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>. We first consider constant step-sizes <math id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}\equiv\beta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}\equiv\beta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{0}\in\{0.1,\ldots,3.0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>3.0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{0}\in\{0.1,\ldots,3.0\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Figure <a href="#S5.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 5.1.1 Markov Reward Process ‣ 5.1 Policy Evaluation ‣ 5 Numerical Experiments ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> summarizes the results
(solid line = mean, shaded band = 95<math id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>%</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\%</annotation></semantics></math> confidence interval). As shown in the left panel, the average
loss across 50 independent experiments increases for all methods as <math id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> becomes larger, around
<math id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{0}\approx 0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{0}\approx 0.3</annotation></semantics></math> or more. However, as <math id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{0}\to 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{0}\to 2</annotation></semantics></math>, standard average-reward TD(<math id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) becomes
unstable and its loss explodes, whereas average-reward implicit TD(<math id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) remains numerically stable
with modest loss growth. To compare all four algorithms’ behavior at a moderate step-size, the right
panel fixes a step-size value <math id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{0}=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{0}=1.0</annotation></semantics></math> and tracks performance over iterations: average-reward
implicit TD(<math id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) maintains relatively low error throughout, while standard average-reward
TD(<math id="S5.SS1.SSS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) incurs substantially larger error over the horizon.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F2" class="ltx_figure">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 2</span>: </span><span id="S5.F2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">MRP experiment under constant step-size, with exponential weighting parameter and
step-size ratio set to <math id="S5.F2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lambda,c_{\alpha})=(0.25,1.0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lambda,c_{\alpha})=(0.25,1.0)</annotation></semantics></math>. The solid line represents the mean, and the
shaded region denotes the 95% confidence interval. (Left) Loss value from step-size 0.1 to 3.0. (Right)
Loss value over iterations with initial step-size <math id="S5.F2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{0}=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{0}=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.
</span></figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S5.F2.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.06149v1/figure/MRP/constant/summary_plot_CUT_lamb0.25_alpha1.00.png" id="S5.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/417;" width="476" height="417" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S5.F2.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.06149v1/figure/MRP/constant/alpha_1.0_full.png" id="S5.F2.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/417;" width="476" height="417" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.1.2 </span>Average-Reward Boyan Chain</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We next study the average-reward Boyan chain under deterministic policies. As in the MRP setting, the
Boyan chain is a standard benchmark for TD learning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>. Because the original
formulation is not average-reward, we use the variant proposed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>]</cite>, which has 13
states and 2 actions. In each experiment, we construct a deterministic policy by assigning an action to
each state via independent <math id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Bernoulli}(0.5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Bernoulli</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Bernoulli}(0.5)</annotation></semantics></math> draws. As with the MRP experiments, we assess
performance using the average loss across 50 independent runs. Figure <a href="#S5.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 5.1.2 Average-Reward Boyan Chain ‣ 5.1 Policy Evaluation ‣ 5 Numerical Experiments ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>
shows results on the Boyan chain example under the decaying step-size schedule <math id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}=\beta_{0}/(t+1)^{0.99}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>0.99</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}=\beta_{0}/(t+1)^{0.99}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the left panel, average-reward implicit TD(<math id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) methods remain stable
across <math id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{0}\in[0.1,3.0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3.0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{0}\in[0.1,3.0]</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas the standard average-reward TD(<math id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) becomes unstable and
its loss grows rapidly as <math id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> approaches <math id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.5</annotation></semantics></math>. The right panel displays learning curves for
<math id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}=1.5/(t+1)^{0.99}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>0.99</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}=1.5/(t+1)^{0.99}</annotation></semantics></math> over 2000 iterations. The loss of standard average-reward TD(<math id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>)
method consistently exceeds that of the average-reward implicit TD(<math id="S5.SS1.SSS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) methods, highlighting the
latter’s improved numerical stability and superior performance.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F3" class="ltx_figure">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 3</span>: </span><span id="S5.F3.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Boyan experiment with exponential weighting parameter and step-size ratio set to <math id="S5.F3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lambda,c_{\alpha})=(0.25,1.0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lambda,c_{\alpha})=(0.25,1.0)</annotation></semantics></math> under decaying step-size schedule <math id="S5.F3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}=\beta_{0}/(t+1)^{0.99}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>0.99</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}=\beta_{0}/(t+1)^{0.99}</annotation></semantics></math>. Solid lines denote the mean, and shaded regions represent 95% confidence intervals. (Left) Loss value with initial step-sizes ranging from 0.1 to 3.0.
(Right) Loss value over iterations with initial step-size <math id="S5.F3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{0}=1.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{0}=1.5</annotation></semantics></math>. </span></figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S5.F3.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.06149v1/figure/Boyan/s_decay/summary_plot_CUT_lamb0.25_alpha1.00.png" id="S5.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/417;" width="476" height="417" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S5.F3.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.06149v1/figure/Boyan/s_decay/alpha_1.5_full.png" id="S5.F3.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/417;" width="476" height="417" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Control Experiments</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we utilize the proposed average-reward implicit TD(<math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) on control tasks. We use state–action–reward–state–action (SARSA) with linear function approximation to estimate the action-value function. Each experiment comprises <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=15000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=15000</annotation></semantics></math> time steps and is repeated over 30 independent runs. We employ a decaying step-size schedule <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}=\beta_{0}/(t+400)^{0.99}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>400</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>0.99</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}=\beta_{0}/(t+400)^{0.99}</annotation></semantics></math>, holding <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> constant for the first 150 iterations to encourage early exploration before gradually reducing it thereafter.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.2.1 </span>Access-Control Queuing</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We study the canonical access-control queuing problem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite> in the average-reward setting. At each decision epoch, an arriving customer belongs to one of four equiprobable classes, and the agent chooses whether to admit or reject the customer. There are ten identical servers; if admitted, the customer yields an immediate reward and occupies a server. Service completion occurs independently at each step with a fixed probability, inducing stochastic transitions in server availability. The goal is to learn an admission policy that optimally maps the current customer class and the number of available servers to an admit/reject decision. We illustrate average-reward learning results in the left panel of Figure <a href="#S5.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 5.2.1 Access-Control Queuing ‣ 5.2 Control Experiments ‣ 5 Numerical Experiments ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. The average-reward implicit TD(<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) methods consistently outperform the average-reward TD(<math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) method across varying initial step-sizes in terms of average-reward. As the initial step-size increases, the implicit methods show a mild performance gain and remain stable whereas standard version deteriorates and fails to benefit from larger steps.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F4" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_center">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="S5.F4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Control experiment with exponential weighting parameter and step-size ratio parameter <math id="S5.F4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lambda,c_{\alpha})=(0.25,1.0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lambda,c_{\alpha})=(0.25,1.0)</annotation></semantics></math>, under the decaying step-size schedule <math id="S5.F4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}=\beta_{0}/(t+400)^{0.99}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>400</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>0.99</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}=\beta_{0}/(t+400)^{0.99}</annotation></semantics></math>. Initial step-size ranges from 0.25 to 1.5. Solid lines denote the mean, and shaded regions represent 95% confidence intervals.</span></figcaption><img src="2510.06149v1/figure/access_control/s_decay/combo_FULL_lamb0.25_alpha1.00.png" id="S5.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/268;" width="476" height="268" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.2.2 </span>Pendulum Environment</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We also apply the proposed average-reward implicit TD(<math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) to the <span id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Pendulum-v1</span> environment. Because the environment is defined with episodic terminations <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite>, we modify it to match the infinite-horizon average-reward setting. The control objective is to keep the pendulum upright. The right panel of Figure <a href="#S5.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 5.2.1 Access-Control Queuing ‣ 5.2 Control Experiments ‣ 5 Numerical Experiments ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> shows results for the pendulum environment with <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lambda,c_{\alpha})=(0.25,1.0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lambda,c_{\alpha})=(0.25,1.0)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Mirroring the access-control task, larger initial step-sizes benefit the average-reward implicit TD(<math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) methods, which achieve higher average reward and remain stable, whereas standard average-reward TD(<math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) fails to benefit from larger step-sizes and exhibits no improvement.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We introduced average-reward implicit TD(<math id="S6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>), a fixed-point variant of the average reward TD(<math id="S6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) that preserves per iteration complexity while markedly improving stability to step-size choices. Our theoretical guarantees provide explicit finite-time error bounds under both constant and decaying step-sizes, established via a projection-based analysis. Across policy evaluation and control examples, the implicit updates deliver robust performance over a wide range of step-sizes, demonstrating strong practical performance consistent with the theory. Looking ahead, promising directions include a full theoretical analysis of average-reward implicit SARSA and rigorous two-time-scale extensions of both standard and implicit average-reward TD(<math id="S6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>). A related direction is to build implicit TD methods to estimate the asymptotic variance of cumulative reward in the average-reward regime.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>List of notations</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To provide rigorous details behind the established theoretical results, we provide a summary of the necessary assumptions, notations, and facts.</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}=\{1,\cdots,|\mathcal{S}|\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}=\{1,\cdots,|\mathcal{S}|\}</annotation></semantics></math>: state space</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{S^{\mu}_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{S^{\mu}_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math>: a sequence of states under policy <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A^{\mu}_{t})_{t\in\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A^{\mu}_{t})_{t\in\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math>: a sequence of actions under policy <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\mu}_{t}:=\mu(S^{\mu}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\mu}_{t}:=\mu(S^{\mu}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(R^{\mu}_{t})_{t\in\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(R^{\mu}_{t})_{t\in\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math>: a sequence of rewards under policy <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\mu}_{t}=r(S^{\mu}_{t},A^{\mu}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\mu}_{t}=r(S^{\mu}_{t},A^{\mu}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p^{\mu}\left(S^{\mu}_{t+1}|S^{\mu}_{t}\right):=p\left\{S^{\mu}_{t+1}|S^{\mu}_{t},A^{\mu}_{t}=\mu(S^{\mu}_{t})\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\mu}\left(S^{\mu}_{t+1}|S^{\mu}_{t}\right):=p\left\{S^{\mu}_{t+1}|S^{\mu}_{t},A^{\mu}_{t}=\mu(S^{\mu}_{t})\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>: transition probabilities under policy <math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{P}^{\mu}=\bigl[P^{\mu}_{ij}\bigr]_{i,j=1}^{|\mathcal{S}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{P}^{\mu}=\bigl[P^{\mu}_{ij}\bigr]_{i,j=1}^{|\mathcal{S}|}</annotation></semantics></math>: time-homogeneous transition probability matrix with
<math id="A1.I1.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\mu}_{ij}=p^{\mu}\left\{S^{\mu}_{t+1}=j\mid S^{\mu}_{t}=i\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\mu}_{ij}=p^{\mu}\left\{S^{\mu}_{t+1}=j\mid S^{\mu}_{t}=i\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mu}=(\pi^{\mu}_{i})_{i=1}^{|\mathcal{S}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mu}=(\pi^{\mu}_{i})_{i=1}^{|\mathcal{S}|}</annotation></semantics></math>: a unique stationary distribution of <math id="A1.I1.i7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{S^{\mu}_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{S^{\mu}_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{r}^{\mu}=\left[r\{1,\mu(1)\},\cdots,r\{|\mathcal{S}|,\mu(|\mathcal{S}|)\}\right]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒓</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{r}^{\mu}=\left[r\{1,\mu(1)\},\cdots,r\{|\mathcal{S}|,\mu(|\mathcal{S}|)\}\right]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>: a reward vector under policy <math id="A1.I1.i8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i9" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}^{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>: expectation with respect to the Markov chain <math id="A1.I1.i9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{S^{\mu}_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{S^{\mu}_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> with a fixed initial state <math id="A1.I1.i9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\mu}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\mu}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i10" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}^{\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mu}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}^{\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mu}}</annotation></semantics></math>: expectation with respect to the stationary distribution of the Markov chain <math id="A1.I1.i10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{S^{\mu}_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{S^{\mu}_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i11" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i11.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|</annotation></semantics></math>: Euclidean norm for vectors and the induced operator norm for matrices</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i12" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lesssim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≲</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lesssim</annotation></semantics></math>: inequality up to a constant</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i13" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i13.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\boldsymbol{X}_{t}:=\left(S^{\mu}_{t},S^{\mu}_{t+1},\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\right),\quad\boldsymbol{X}_{t-\tau:t}=(S^{\mu}_{t},S^{\mu}_{t+1},\boldsymbol{z}_{t-\tau:t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{X}_{t}:=\left(S^{\mu}_{t},S^{\mu}_{t+1},\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\right),\quad\boldsymbol{X}_{t-\tau:t}=(S^{\mu}_{t},S^{\mu}_{t+1},\boldsymbol{z}_{t-\tau:t})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i14" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\phi}_{l}=\boldsymbol{\phi}(S^{\mu}_{l}),\quad\|\boldsymbol{\phi}_{l}\|\leq 1,\quad\boldsymbol{\Phi}\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{S}|\times d}:" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\phi}_{l}=\boldsymbol{\phi}(S^{\mu}_{l}),\quad\|\boldsymbol{\phi}_{l}\|\leq 1,\quad\boldsymbol{\Phi}\in\mathbb{R}^{|\mathcal{S}|\times d}:</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A1.I1.i14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">feature
matrix whose <math id="A1.I1.i14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i^{\text{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>i</mi><mtext>th</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{\text{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> row is</span> <math id="A1.I1.i14.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\phi}(i)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\phi}(i)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i15" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i15.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i15.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i15.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\boldsymbol{z}_{t}=\sum_{l=0}^{t}\lambda^{t-l}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{l},\quad\boldsymbol{z}_{t-\tau:t}=\sum_{l=t-\tau}^{t}\lambda^{t-l}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{l},\quad\omega^{\mu}=\lim_{T\to\infty}\frac{1}{T}\mathbb{E}^{\mu}\left(\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}R^{\mu}_{t}\right)={\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mu}}^{\top}\boldsymbol{r}^{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝝅</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>μ</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><msup><mi>𝒓</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{z}_{t}=\sum_{l=0}^{t}\lambda^{t-l}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{l},\quad\boldsymbol{z}_{t-\tau:t}=\sum_{l=t-\tau}^{t}\lambda^{t-l}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{l},\quad\omega^{\mu}=\lim_{T\to\infty}\frac{1}{T}\mathbb{E}^{\mu}\left(\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}R^{\mu}_{t}\right)={\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mu}}^{\top}\boldsymbol{r}^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i16" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i16.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i16.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i16.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\mathbb{O}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝕆</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\mathbb{O}}</annotation></semantics></math>: projection operator onto <math id="A1.I1.i16.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{O}:=\mathbb{S}_{\boldsymbol{\Phi},\boldsymbol{e}}^{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕆</mi><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒆</mi></mrow><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{O}:=\mathbb{S}_{\boldsymbol{\Phi},\boldsymbol{e}}^{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> where
<math id="A1.I1.i16.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{\boldsymbol{\Phi},\boldsymbol{e}}:=\operatorname{span}\{\boldsymbol{\theta}:\boldsymbol{\Phi}\boldsymbol{\theta}=\boldsymbol{e}\},\quad\boldsymbol{\Pi}:=\begin{bmatrix}1&amp;0\\
0&amp;\Pi_{\mathbb{O}}\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒆</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>span</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒆</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝚷</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝕆</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{\boldsymbol{\Phi},\boldsymbol{e}}:=\operatorname{span}\{\boldsymbol{\theta}:\boldsymbol{\Phi}\boldsymbol{\theta}=\boldsymbol{e}\},\quad\boldsymbol{\Pi}:=\begin{bmatrix}1&amp;0\\
0&amp;\Pi_{\mathbb{O}}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i17" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i17.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i17.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{A}_{t}=\boldsymbol{A}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t}):=\begin{bmatrix}-c_{\alpha}&amp;0\\
-\boldsymbol{z}_{t}&{\boldsymbol{z}_{t}}(\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top})\end{bmatrix},\quad\boldsymbol{A}:=\mathbb{E}^{\pi^{\mu}}\boldsymbol{A}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{A}_{t}=\boldsymbol{A}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t}):=\begin{bmatrix}-c_{\alpha}&amp;0\\
-\boldsymbol{z}_{t}&amp;{\boldsymbol{z}_{t}}(\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top})\end{bmatrix},\quad\boldsymbol{A}:=\mathbb{E}^{\pi^{\mu}}\boldsymbol{A}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i18" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i18.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i18.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i18.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\boldsymbol{A}_{t-\tau:t}=\boldsymbol{A}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t-\tau:t}):=\begin{bmatrix}-c_{\alpha}&amp;0\\
-\boldsymbol{z}_{t-\tau:t}&{\boldsymbol{z}_{t-\tau:t}}(\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top})\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{A}_{t-\tau:t}=\boldsymbol{A}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t-\tau:t}):=\begin{bmatrix}-c_{\alpha}&amp;0\\
-\boldsymbol{z}_{t-\tau:t}&amp;{\boldsymbol{z}_{t-\tau:t}}(\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top})\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i19" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i19.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i19.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i19.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\boldsymbol{b}_{t}=\boldsymbol{\boldsymbol{b}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t})}:=\begin{bmatrix}c_{\alpha}R^{\mu}_{t}\\
R^{\mu}_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\end{bmatrix},\quad\boldsymbol{b}=\mathbb{E}^{\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mu}}\boldsymbol{b}_{t},\quad\boldsymbol{b}_{t-\tau:t}=\boldsymbol{b}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t-\tau:t}):=\begin{bmatrix}c_{\alpha}R^{\mu}_{t}\\
R^{\mu}_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t-\tau:t}\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒃</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒃</mi><mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>𝒕</mi></msub><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup></msup><msub><mi>𝒃</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝒃</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>R</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{b}_{t}=\boldsymbol{\boldsymbol{b}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t})}:=\begin{bmatrix}c_{\alpha}R^{\mu}_{t}\\
R^{\mu}_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\end{bmatrix},\quad\boldsymbol{b}=\mathbb{E}^{\boldsymbol{\pi}^{\mu}}\boldsymbol{b}_{t},\quad\boldsymbol{b}_{t-\tau:t}=\boldsymbol{b}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t-\tau:t}):=\begin{bmatrix}c_{\alpha}R^{\mu}_{t}\\
R^{\mu}_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t-\tau:t}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i20" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i20.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i20.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i20.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}:=\begin{bmatrix}\widehat{\omega}_{t}\\
\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\end{bmatrix},\quad\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{*}=\begin{bmatrix}\omega^{\mu}\\
\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}\end{bmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>ω</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝕆</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}:=\begin{bmatrix}\widehat{\omega}_{t}\\
\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\end{bmatrix},\quad\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{*}=\begin{bmatrix}\omega^{\mu}\\
\boldsymbol{\theta}^{*}\end{bmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{O}</annotation></semantics></math> is the unique element satisfying <math id="A1.I1.i20.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{A}\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{*}=\boldsymbol{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒃</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{A}\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{*}=\boldsymbol{b}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i21" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i21.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i21.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i21.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{D}_{t}:=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{1}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}&amp;0\\
0&amp;\frac{1}{1+\beta_{t}||\boldsymbol{z}_{t}||^{2}}\boldsymbol{I}_{d}\end{bmatrix},\quad\underline{\boldsymbol{D}_{t}}:=\gamma_{t}\boldsymbol{I}_{d+1},\quad\gamma_{t}=\min\left(\frac{1}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}},\frac{(1-\lambda)^{2}}{(1-\lambda)^{2}+\beta_{t}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mi>𝑫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{D}_{t}:=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{1}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}&amp;0\\
0&amp;\frac{1}{1+\beta_{t}||\boldsymbol{z}_{t}||^{2}}\boldsymbol{I}_{d}\end{bmatrix},\quad\underline{\boldsymbol{D}_{t}}:=\gamma_{t}\boldsymbol{I}_{d+1},\quad\gamma_{t}=\min\left(\frac{1}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}},\frac{(1-\lambda)^{2}}{(1-\lambda)^{2}+\beta_{t}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i22" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i22.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i22.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i22.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{t}(\boldsymbol{\Theta},\boldsymbol{X}_{t}):=\left\langle\left(\boldsymbol{A}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t})-\boldsymbol{A}\right)\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}},\underline{\boldsymbol{D}_{t}}(\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}-\boldsymbol{\Theta})\right\rangle+\left\langle\boldsymbol{b}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t})-\boldsymbol{b},\underline{\boldsymbol{D}_{t}}(\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}-\boldsymbol{\Theta})\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mi>𝑫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝚯</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒃</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mi>𝑫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝚯</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{t}(\boldsymbol{\Theta},\boldsymbol{X}_{t}):=\left\langle\left(\boldsymbol{A}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t})-\boldsymbol{A}\right)\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}},\underline{\boldsymbol{D}_{t}}(\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}-\boldsymbol{\Theta})\right\rangle+\left\langle\boldsymbol{b}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t})-\boldsymbol{b},\underline{\boldsymbol{D}_{t}}(\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}-\boldsymbol{\Theta})\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i23" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i23.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i23.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i23.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{t}(\boldsymbol{\Theta},\boldsymbol{X}_{t}):=(\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}-\boldsymbol{\Theta})^{\top}\left(\boldsymbol{A}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t})^{\top}-\boldsymbol{A}^{\top}\right)\underline{\boldsymbol{D}_{t}}\left(\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}-\boldsymbol{\Theta}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝚯</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mi>𝑫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝚯</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{t}(\boldsymbol{\Theta},\boldsymbol{X}_{t}):=(\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}-\boldsymbol{\Theta})^{\top}\left(\boldsymbol{A}(\boldsymbol{X}_{t})^{\top}-\boldsymbol{A}^{\top}\right)\underline{\boldsymbol{D}_{t}}\left(\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}-\boldsymbol{\Theta}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i24" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i24.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i24.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i24.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{M}=\text{diag}\left(\pi^{\mu}_{1},\cdots,\pi^{\mu}_{|\mathcal{S}|}\right),\quad\Delta:=\min_{\|\boldsymbol{\theta}\|=1,\boldsymbol{\theta}\in\mathbb{O}}\boldsymbol{\theta}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\boldsymbol{\Phi}}^{\top}\boldsymbol{M}\left\{\boldsymbol{I}-(1-\lambda)\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}\lambda^{m}(\boldsymbol{P}^{\mu})^{m+1}\right\}\boldsymbol{\boldsymbol{\Phi}}\boldsymbol{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕆</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{M}=\text{diag}\left(\pi^{\mu}_{1},\cdots,\pi^{\mu}_{|\mathcal{S}|}\right),\quad\Delta:=\min_{\|\boldsymbol{\theta}\|=1,\boldsymbol{\theta}\in\mathbb{O}}\boldsymbol{\theta}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\boldsymbol{\Phi}}^{\top}\boldsymbol{M}\left\{\boldsymbol{I}-(1-\lambda)\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}\lambda^{m}(\boldsymbol{P}^{\mu})^{m+1}\right\}\boldsymbol{\boldsymbol{\Phi}}\boldsymbol{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Theoretical results</h2>

<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The implicit update rule is</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\frac{\beta_{t}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\frac{\beta_{t}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\frac{c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\frac{c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span> We first revisit the recursion formula in (<a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3 Average-Reward Implicit TD(𝜆) ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) and (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3 Average-Reward Implicit TD(𝜆) ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) :</p>
<table id="A2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\lambda\boldsymbol{z}_{t-1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{z}_{t}^{\top}{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}})\boldsymbol{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\lambda\boldsymbol{z}_{t-1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{z}_{t}^{\top}{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}})\boldsymbol{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{\omega}_{t}+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}(R^{\mu}_{t}-{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{\omega}_{t}+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}(R^{\mu}_{t}-{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Our goal is to derive the update rule for <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\omega}</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be done by combining <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1},\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1},\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(1) Update Rule for <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math></h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let us first examine the update rule for the parameter <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining the rightmost term to the left, we have</p>
<table id="A2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\left(\boldsymbol{I}+\beta_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}^{\top}\right)\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}&amp;=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\lambda\boldsymbol{z}_{t-1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\left(\boldsymbol{I}+\beta_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}^{\top}\right)\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}&amp;=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\lambda\boldsymbol{z}_{t-1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">From the Woodbury matrix identity <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\boldsymbol{I}+\beta_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}^{\top}\right)^{-1}=\boldsymbol{I}-\frac{\beta_{t}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\boldsymbol{I}+\beta_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}^{\top}\right)^{-1}=\boldsymbol{I}-\frac{\beta_{t}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\lambda\boldsymbol{z}_{t-1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}-\frac{\beta_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}-\beta_{t}\frac{\beta_{t}R^{\mu}_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}+\beta_{t}\frac{\beta_{t}\widehat{\omega}_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\lambda\boldsymbol{z}_{t-1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}-\frac{\beta_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}-\beta_{t}\frac{\beta_{t}R^{\mu}_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}+\beta_{t}\frac{\beta_{t}\widehat{\omega}_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\beta_{t}\frac{\beta_{t}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}-\beta_{t}\frac{\beta_{t}\lambda\boldsymbol{z}_{t-1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\beta_{t}\frac{\beta_{t}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}-\beta_{t}\frac{\beta_{t}\lambda\boldsymbol{z}_{t-1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}R^{\mu}_{t}\left(1-\frac{\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}-\beta_{t}\widehat{\omega}_{t}\left(1-\frac{\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}R^{\mu}_{t}\left(1-\frac{\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}-\beta_{t}\widehat{\omega}_{t}\left(1-\frac{\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\beta_{t}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\left(1-\frac{\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}+\beta_{t}\lambda\boldsymbol{z}_{t-1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\left(1-\frac{\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}-\frac{\beta_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\beta_{t}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\left(1-\frac{\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}+\beta_{t}\lambda\boldsymbol{z}_{t-1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\left(1-\frac{\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}-\frac{\beta_{t}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\boldsymbol{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\frac{\beta_{t}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\lambda\boldsymbol{z}_{t-1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{z}_{t}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\frac{\beta_{t}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\lambda\boldsymbol{z}_{t-1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{z}_{t}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\frac{\beta_{t}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\frac{\beta_{t}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(2) Update Rule for <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\omega}</annotation></semantics></math></h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly, for the update rule for the <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\omega}</annotation></semantics></math>, we combine the term to the left hand side, which yields</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t})\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}=\widehat{\omega}_{t}+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}R^{\mu}_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t})\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}=\widehat{\omega}_{t}+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}R^{\mu}_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Now, dividing with <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> we have</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}=\frac{1}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\frac{c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}R^{\mu}_{t}=\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\frac{c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}=\frac{1}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\frac{c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}R^{\mu}_{t}=\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\frac{c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This completes the whole update rules.
 ∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Proof of Main Theorems</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide a proof of the finite-time error bounds of the projected average-reward projected TD(<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) algorithm. To this end, recall that the implicit average-reward TD(<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) update rule is given by</p>
<table id="A2.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\frac{c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\frac{c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\frac{\beta_{t}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\frac{\beta_{t}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">To gain numerical stability as well as to facilitate theoretical analysis, we impose additional projection steps to both the primary iterate <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and the reward iterate <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\omega}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\omega}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall that the projection operator with a radius <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="A2.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{R}(\boldsymbol{u})=\begin{cases}\boldsymbol{u},\quad\quad\text{if}~\|\boldsymbol{u}\|\leq R\\
\frac{R}{\|\boldsymbol{u}\|}\boldsymbol{u}\quad\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒖</mi><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{R}(\boldsymbol{u})=\begin{cases}\boldsymbol{u},\quad\quad\text{if}~\|\boldsymbol{u}\|\leq R\\
\frac{R}{\|\boldsymbol{u}\|}\boldsymbol{u}\quad\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Then the projected average-reward TD(<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) update is as follows</p>
<table id="A2.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Pi_{R_{\omega}}\left\{\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\frac{c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}\right)\right\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Pi_{R_{\omega}}\left\{\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\frac{c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}\right)\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Pi_{R_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}}\left\{\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\frac{\beta_{t}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\right\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Pi_{R_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}}\left\{\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\frac{\beta_{t}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\omega}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\omega}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> are large enough such that <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\omega}\geq\|\omega^{\mu}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mi>μ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\omega}\geq\|\omega^{\mu}\|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\geq\|\boldsymbol{\theta^{*}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\geq\|\boldsymbol{\theta^{*}}\|</annotation></semantics></math>. Following the analysis of the average-reward TD(<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>) in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>, we consider the following auxiliary iterates</p>
<table id="A2.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\omega}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Pi_{R_{\omega}}\left\{\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\frac{c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}\right)\right\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Pi_{R_{\omega}}\left\{\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\frac{c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}{1+c_{\alpha}\beta_{t}}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}\right)\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Pi_{\mathbb{O}}\left[\Pi_{R_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}}\left\{\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\frac{\beta_{t}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\right\}\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝕆</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>μ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Pi_{\mathbb{O}}\left[\Pi_{R_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}}\left\{\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}+\frac{\beta_{t}}{1+\beta_{t}\|\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\|^{2}}\left(R^{\mu}_{t}-\widehat{\omega}_{t}+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t+1}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}_{t}\right)\boldsymbol{z}_{t}\right\}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">to facilitate finite-time error analysis. Here, the space <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{O}</annotation></semantics></math> is the orthogonal complement of the space generated by <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta_{e}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>𝒆</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta_{e}}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Phi}\boldsymbol{\theta_{e}}=\boldsymbol{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>𝒆</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒆</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Phi}\boldsymbol{\theta_{e}}=\boldsymbol{e}</annotation></semantics></math>. In short, when considering the primary iterate, any deviance in the direction of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta_{e}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>𝒆</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta_{e}}</annotation></semantics></math> will be ignored under <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\mathbb{O}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝕆</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\mathbb{O}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the matrix notations we introduced, we can now succinctly write both (<a href="#A2.E7" title="In B.1 Proof of Main Theorems ‣ Appendix B Theoretical results ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) and (<a href="#A2.E8" title="In B.1 Proof of Main Theorems ‣ Appendix B Theoretical results ‣ Implicit Updates for Average-Reward Temporal Difference Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) as</p>
<table id="A2.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t+1}=\boldsymbol{\Pi}\left[\Pi_{R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}\left\{\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}\boldsymbol{D}_{t}\left(\boldsymbol{A_{t}}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\boldsymbol{b}_{t}\right)\right\}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝚷</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>𝒕</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝒃</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t+1}=\boldsymbol{\Pi}\left[\Pi_{R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}\left\{\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}\boldsymbol{D}_{t}\left(\boldsymbol{A_{t}}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\boldsymbol{b}_{t}\right)\right\}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">where
<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}(\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}):=\left[\Pi_{R_{\omega}}(\widehat{\omega}),\Pi_{R_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}}(\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}})\right]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}(\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}):=\left[\Pi_{R_{\omega}}(\widehat{\omega}),\Pi_{R_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}}(\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}})\right]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}=[\widehat{\omega},\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}=[\widehat{\omega},\widehat{\boldsymbol{\theta}}]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}=\sqrt{R_{\omega}^{2}+R^{2}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}=\sqrt{R_{\omega}^{2}+R^{2}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}=\boldsymbol{\Pi}\left(\Pi_{R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝚷</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}=\boldsymbol{\Pi}\left(\Pi_{R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A2.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}-\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t+1}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}-\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t+1}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\|\boldsymbol{\Pi}\left(\Pi_{R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}\right)-\boldsymbol{\Pi}\left[\Pi_{R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}\left\{\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}\boldsymbol{D}_{t}\left(\boldsymbol{A}_{t}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\boldsymbol{b}_{t}\right)\right\}\right]\right\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚷</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚷</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝒃</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\|\boldsymbol{\Pi}\left(\Pi_{R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}\right)-\boldsymbol{\Pi}\left[\Pi_{R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}\left\{\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}\boldsymbol{D}_{t}\left(\boldsymbol{A}_{t}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\boldsymbol{b}_{t}\right)\right\}\right]\right\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left\|\Pi_{R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}-\Pi_{R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}\left\{\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}\boldsymbol{D}_{t}\left(\boldsymbol{A_{t}}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\boldsymbol{b}_{t}\right)\right\}\right\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>𝒕</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝒃</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left\|\Pi_{R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}-\Pi_{R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}\left\{\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}\boldsymbol{D}_{t}\left(\boldsymbol{A_{t}}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\boldsymbol{b}_{t}\right)\right\}\right\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left\|\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}-\left[\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}\boldsymbol{D}_{t}\left(\boldsymbol{A}_{t}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\boldsymbol{b}_{t}\right)\right]\right\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝒃</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left\|\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}-\left[\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\beta_{t}\boldsymbol{D}_{t}\left(\boldsymbol{A}_{t}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\boldsymbol{b}_{t}\right)\right]\right\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left\|\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}-\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}\right\|^{2}\underbrace{-2\beta_{t}\left[\boldsymbol{D}_{t}\left(\boldsymbol{A}_{t}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\boldsymbol{b}_{t}\right)\right]^{\top}\left(\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}-\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}\right)}_{(*)}+\underbrace{\beta_{t}^{2}\left\|\boldsymbol{D}_{t}\left(\boldsymbol{A}_{t}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\boldsymbol{b}_{t}\right)\right\|^{2}}_{(**)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝒃</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝒃</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></munder><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left\|\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}-\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}\right\|^{2}\underbrace{-2\beta_{t}\left[\boldsymbol{D}_{t}\left(\boldsymbol{A}_{t}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\boldsymbol{b}_{t}\right)\right]^{\top}\left(\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}-\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}\right)}_{(*)}+\underbrace{\beta_{t}^{2}\left\|\boldsymbol{D}_{t}\left(\boldsymbol{A}_{t}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}+\boldsymbol{b}_{t}\right)\right\|^{2}}_{(**)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.7" class="ltx_p">where the first inequality is due to non-expansiveness of the operator <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚷</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math> and the second inequality is due to non-expansiveness of the projection operator <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{R_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We first obtain an upper bound of the expression in <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(*)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(*)</annotation></semantics></math>. To this end, note that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(*)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(*)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-2\beta_{t}\left\{\boldsymbol{D}_{t}\left(\boldsymbol{A}_{t}\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}-\boldsymbol{A}_{t}\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}+\boldsymbol{A}_{t}\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}-\boldsymbol{A}\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}+\boldsymbol{A}\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}+\boldsymbol{b}_{t}\right)\right\}^{\top}\left(\boldsymbol{\Theta^{*}}-\widehat{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}_{t}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝒃</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo><